@@ -70,6 +70,22 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to :meth:`~rich.console.Console.print` and :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log`. It converts each object to a string with ``str()``, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result as plain text followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("foo", "bar", sep=".", end="!\n")
+
+``out`` does the following:
+
+* Writes the text as given, with no pretty printing of containers.
+* Does not wrap, crop, or ignore the console width.
+* Does not apply console markup or replace emoji codes.
+* Applies highlighting by default. Set ``highlight=False`` to disable it, or ``highlight=None`` to use the console default.
+* Accepts a basic ``style``, applied in the same way as :meth:`~rich.console.Console.print`.
+
+
